  "disposition": "ADMIT_BYTE_WEIGHT_AS_DISTINCT_ARCHIVE_LAYER",
  "verified": "Of 38 action-to-product rank reversals, 35 persist under byte totals and three are undone; byte weighting creates 24 additional reversals, yielding 59. Byte prominence therefore combines protocol-derived products/action with a distinct mean-bytes/product layer.",
  "decision_use": "Use products to reason about protocol-derived sample weight and bytes to reason about retrieval or systems burden. Neither is a neutral proxy for observations, and byte size is not a quality score.",
  "pixel_payload_bytes": 0,
  "claim_ceiling": "Stage 11K may establish that among 621 strictly comparable active-window pairs, 35 reverse under both product and byte units, three reverse under products only, 24 reverse under bytes only, and 559 reverse under neither. It may establish the exact identity bytes/action = products/action \u00d7 mean bytes/product and therefore show that byte prominence adds a distinct representation-size weight to protocol-derived product multiplicity. It cannot interpret byte size as quality or scientific importance, assert an actual sampler or observed model bias, infer a causal outcome effect, nominate a universal correction, recommend deletion, extend beyond admitted active windows, or make a novelty, priority, or physical-science claim.",
  "next_step_logic": {
    "if_public_analysis_is_selected": "Use product counts to explain protocol-derived sample weighting and bytes to explain retrieval burden; do not collapse the two into one mechanism.",
    "if_a_model_task_is_selected": "Do not weight examples by storage bytes unless that estimand is explicit; preserve product sizes as metadata for retrieval and systems planning.",
    "if_representation_encoding_or_inventory_changes": "Recompute the byte layer because mean bytes/product may change even when product counts do not.",
    "recheck_trigger": "A revised window set, relationship manifest, representation inventory, encoding policy, or actual sampler."
